  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, but I could not fully check it. `@aura3d/engine` is missing from this sandbox: `node_modules/@aura3d` is empty, so the one remaining typecheck error is \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". The library's types never loaded, so none of my API calls were checked against them, and I never saw the scene render. The code follows `llms.txt` and `docs/agents/api-signatures.md`. The `group(..., {})` call and the custom-shader inputs `modelMatrix` and `cameraPosition` are the parts I'm least sure of. The shading values are untuned guesses.\n\nWhat the scene contains:\n- **Paint:** the body, cabin and roof are procedurally lofted meshes. A custom GLSL material renders the paint with a deep candy-red base layer, fine metallic flakes, and a Fresnel clear coat. The coat mirrors a procedural studio environment of three long strip softboxes (overhead, left and right), a cool blue rim strip and a dim front fill. The reflections bend over the curved panels.\n- **Trim and wheels:** the cabin glass is black glossy. There are two chrome side strips, four rubber wheels with chrome hubs, and visible emissive strip fixtures.\n- **Turntable:** a dark glossy platform with an emissive ring light. A mirrored copy of the car sits under the semi-transparent floor, so the car is faintly reflected.\n- **Motion and state:** the \"turntable\" group rotates at 20°/s while the camera stays fixed at a low front-three-quarter angle. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is `{ turntableAngleDeg, paintFinish: 'clearcoat' }` and updates every frame. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\nI annotated the frame callback as `(f: { dt: number })`, because without the package it would otherwise be an implicit `any`.\n\n",
